---
import MainLayout from "../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout
  title="House Rules | Dining Unhinged"
  description="Learn how Dining Unhinged handles reviews, hosted visits, sponsorships, and editorial independence."
>

<section class="page-header">
  <div class="container">

    <h1>House Rules</h1>

    <p class="lead">
      Dining Unhinged exists for one reason. To publish honest reviews of great
      food, memorable drinks, and the places serving them. These are the rules
      that keep it that way.
    </p>

  </div>
</section>

<section class="policy">

  <article>

    <h2>Independent by Design</h2>

    <p>
      Dining Unhinged accepts invitations and hosted experiences.
      If someone picks up the bill, you'll know.
    </p>

    <p>
      Every sponsored or complimentary visit is clearly disclosed.
    </p>

    <blockquote>
      The bill can be covered. The opinion can't.
    </blockquote>

  </article>

  <article>

    <h2>Hosted Visits</h2>

    <p>
      Restaurants, breweries, wineries, distilleries, cafés, hotels, tourism
      organizations, and food brands occasionally invite Dining Unhinged to
      experience what they have to offer.
    </p>

    <p>
      An invitation does not guarantee coverage.
      It certainly doesn't guarantee praise.
    </p>

  </article>

  <article>

    <h2>Sponsored Content</h2>

    <p>
      From time to time, Dining Unhinged may partner with brands that fit
      the publication.
    </p>

    <p>
      Sponsored content is always identified.
      Sponsored partnerships never influence editorial reviews,
      ratings, rankings, or awards.
    </p>

  </article>

  <article>

    <h2>How Reviews Work</h2>

    <p>
      Every review considers the entire experience.
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>Food</li>
      <li>Drinks</li>
      <li>Service</li>
      <li>Hospitality</li>
      <li>Atmosphere</li>
      <li>Value</li>
      <li>Consistency</li>
      <li>Whether I'd happily spend my own money to come back.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      There's no secret formula.
    </p>

    <p>
      Sometimes a burger deserves five stars.
      Sometimes a tasting menu doesn't.
    </p>

  </article>

  <article>

    <h2>Repeat Offenders</h2>

    <p>
      Repeat Offenders is reserved for places I'd gladly return to without
      needing an excuse.
    </p>

    <p>
      Inclusion can't be purchased.
      It's earned.
      Repeatedly.
    </p>

  </article>

  <article>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>

    <p>
      If factual information is incorrect, including hours, ownership, menu
      items, addresses, or similar details, it will be corrected as quickly as
      possible.
    </p>

    <p>
      Opinions remain opinions.
    </p>

  </article>

  <article>

    <h2>Want Dining Unhinged to Visit?</h2>

    <p>
      Invitations are always welcome.
    </p>

    <p>
      Flattery helps.
      Bribery doesn't.
    </p>

    <p>
      If you've built something worth talking about,
      I'd love to hear from you.
    </p>

  </article>

</section>

</MainLayout>